description:
pkix-lint/src/lib.rs LintProfile trait (lines 858-872):

    pub trait LintProfile: Profile {
        fn lints(&self) -> &[Box<dyn Lint>];
        fn lint_runner(&self) -> LintRunner;
    }

lint_runner() is a required method even though a sound default implementation can be derived from lints():

    fn lint_runner(&self) -> LintRunner {
        // Cannot provide a default because lints() returns &[Box<dyn Lint>] — we
        // cannot clone Box<dyn Lint> without a Clone bound on Lint.
        // However we could provide a default if Lint: Clone, or change lints() to
        // return an iterator of fresh instances.
    }

The current situation forces every implementor to write a boilerplate lint_runner() method that just calls all_lints() (see CabfTlsBrProfile). If the LintProfile contract were redesigned so that lints() returned a factory (e.g., fn lints(&self) -> Vec<Box<dyn Lint>>) rather than a reference to a static pool, a blanket default for lint_runner() would be trivially derivable.

The two methods returning different instances (static OnceLock for lints(), fresh allocation for lint_runner()) is also confusing to implementors and documented awkwardly.

This is a R7 / trait-design finding: requiring a method to be implemented manually when it should have a blanket default (or the two methods should be unified).

Category: R7 (missing Default impl / unnecessary required trait method)
